// EXPECT: [E005]
// SOUNDNESS PAIR for loop_fill_whole_pass.ln. The whole-initialisation fact is only true when
// the loop really covers every element, so the recogniser is deliberately narrow: the range
// must start at 0 and end at the array's own length, and the body must be exactly ONE
// assignment whose target is that array indexed by the loop counter.
//
// Here the range stops at 4 over an 8-element array, so `a[7]` reads storage nothing wrote.
// Each of the other ways to break the pattern is refused the same way and for the same reason:
// a conditional store, a second statement in the body, a different index expression, and a
// loop that fills a different array. Widen any one of those and this program compiles and
// reads uninitialised memory.
func main() i32 {
    var a i32[8]
    for k in 0..4 { a[k] = 7 }
    return a[7]
}
